{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795252048,"nonce":"rfP9RB1E7Q9jZaGoGUkAI7jBy0E=","title":"Serial log missing ~60 s of lines after a watch's lost link","message":"Seen 2026-11-21 on firmware 7e597ed plus the uncommitted missed-connect fix (XIAO ESP32-S3,\nFS-4C02A8 treadmill), during watch affinity test 4: watch C3:A4:A4:0B:3E:75 lost its link\n(0x08, put in a microwave) at 154836.\n\nFrom 154846 to 213046 the monitor shows only these lines:\n\n    I (154846) firmware: watch link lost (reason 0x08): only it may reconnect for 120 s\n    I (154856) firmware: advertising for C3:A4:A4:0B:3E:75 only\n    I (194046) firmware: session: looking for a treadmill\n    I (196116) firmware: session: connecting to D9:59:BB:9B:0A:5D\n    I (196116) firmware: connect D9:59:BB:9B:0A:5D\n    I (196716) NimBLE: ogf=0x08, ocf=0x0022, hci_err=0x21A : BLE_ERR_UNSUPP_REM_FEATURE\n    I (196866) esp32_nimble::client::ble_client: mtu update event; conn_handle=3 mtu=256\n    I (213046) firmware: session: idle (no watch)\n\nExpected but missing:\n- firmware::central: \"disconnecting D9:…\" right after 154846 (it shows up only at 213516),\n  and the scan summary every 10 s (none between 150596 and 220556).\n- firmware::footpod: \"watch connected\" and \"notifications\" for C3's reconnect. The session did\n  get WatchSubscribed at 194046, which is sent right after that log line.\n- firmware: after \"connecting\" at 196116, either \"connected to D9:…, waiting for data\" or\n  \"looking for a treadmill\" when CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS (10 s) runs out.\n\nBehaviour was otherwise correct: the Garmin was refused during grace, C3 got back in, and after\nC3 ended (deliberate) the Garmin connected at 213676.\n\nLikely cause: lines lost on the way to the screen, not a firmware stall. The main loop's own\nlines are missing too, though the main loop was clearly running (it logged at 194, 196 and 213),\nso a stalled central thread can't explain it. Suspect devenv's \"watching N files\" footer\nredrawing over the scrolling espflash monitor output in the terminal.\n\nPossibly the same as an earlier unexplained stall around 486 s on older firmware.\n\nTo confirm: capture the next run with `fw-flash 2\u003e\u00261 | tee fw.log` and repeat the lost-link\ntest. If the file has the same gap, it's a real stall: suspect the central thread stuck in a\nscan or connect await, and the NimBLE host task.","files":null}]}